  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 6a4f1de8e0994cb4aaaa0ccb234f52f2, type: 3}
  m_Name: BatangasGotoDishReflection
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  dishName: Batangas Goto
  dishSprite: {fileID: 0}
  pages:
  - Great work. The bowl in front of you is a small act of care. Chinese congee technique,
    Spanish-era beef, Filipino garnishes,
  - ' all brought together in a dish that families reach for when someone they love
    needs comfort.'
  - The ginger does more than flavour. It warms the body and settles the stomach,
    which is why goto has been a convalescent food for generations.
  - 'They are the Lipa canon, documented in peer-reviewed heritage research, and
    they distinguish a competent lomi from a merely passable one. '
  - The next time you make a bowl for someone who is unwell,
  - ' you are doing what Filipino families have been doing with this dish for nearly
    two centuries.'
